          sample: "The bar chart compares how many students chose four different subjects at one university in 2010 and 2020. Overall, Business was the most popular subject in both years, while Engineering grew the fastest over the decade. In contrast, History became noticeably less popular. In 2010, Business led the chart with about 4,200 students, followed by Computer Science with roughly 3,000. Engineering attracted around 2,400 students, and History was the least chosen subject, at approximately 1,800. By 2020, the picture had changed considerably. Business remained in first place, rising slightly to about 4,500 students. The most dramatic increase was in Computer Science, which almost doubled to nearly 5,800 students, overtaking every other subject. Engineering also grew strongly, reaching about 3,600 students. History, however, fell to just 1,200 students. To summarise, technical and business-related subjects clearly gained popularity between 2010 and 2020, whereas interest in History declined, suggesting that students increasingly choose subjects they believe will lead directly to employment. It is also worth noting that the combined total for the four subjects rose from about 11,400 students in 2010 to roughly 15,500 in 2020."
